        "s": {
          "s": [
            {
              "value": [
                "// Regression fixture for issues/03-cqf-parity-gaps.md C2 / C5 / C6.\n//\n// Three operator-lowering rules the HEDIS comparison flagged:\n//   - `in` promotes its right operand with ToList only when that operand does\n//     not already satisfy an In overload for the left operand's type. A\n//     reference to a list- or interval-valued define must not be promoted.\n//   - `during` / `included in` select In (ProperIn) for a point left operand\n//     and IncludedIn (ProperIncludedIn) for an interval one.\n//   - `!=` and `!~` have no ELM operator of their own; they lower to\n//     Not(Equal(...)) and Not(Equivalent(...)).\nlibrary MembershipOperators version '1.0'"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "Annotation"
      }
    ],
